WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:29.019
Thank you. This report covers how NHS England
is doing against its business priorities,

00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:36.699
and against its corporate operations, as well.
Firstly, just a reminder obviously: we in

00:00:36.699 --> 00:00:43.159
our business plan had ten business priorities
that we are going to deliver against this

00:00:43.159 --> 00:00:48.589
year, and those are strongly aligned to and
supportive of the Five-Year Forward View;

00:00:48.589 --> 00:00:53.689
so closely integrated with those, but obviously
they do not include the whole of the Five-Year

00:00:53.689 --> 00:01:00.780
Forward View, which is a responsibility of
the wider system.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:06.720
End of quarter one, we have been going through
with each of those priorities, stock-takes,

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:12.229
to make sure that all the right mechanisms
and processes and leadership and resources

00:01:12.229 --> 00:01:19.870
and funds and activity are in place to give
us assurance around delivery for each of those

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:25.180
priorities. Obviously some are in better shape
than others, reflecting the fact that some

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:31.380
have been reflecting work that has been going
on for some time while some is relatively

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:39.070
new work, and reflecting progress against
delivery of activity with also the inherent

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:44.920
risk and difficulty associated with some of
these, which are massive. We have obviously

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:52.299
had two reports today on cancer and learning
disabilities, which both have massive implications

00:01:52.299 --> 00:02:02.659
for the wider system, which are inherently
difficult to deliver. The RAG ratings there

00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:09.720
reflect those differences, and we will continue
to track progress on each of these throughout

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:16.370
the year. I am not wanting to worry anybody
at this stage about the progress, as I actually

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:23.750
think good arrangements are in place with
most of these.

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:27.709
Probably one other thing to say about the
process that we have been through, because

00:02:27.709 --> 00:02:32.020
I think it is very relevant to discussions
that we have had. As we have gone through

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:40.930
the stock-takes with representatives from
all of NHS England participating in the oversight

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:48.380
groups, it has been a fantastic greater sense
of collaboration across the whole organisation,

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:54.860
with all of us owning all of the priorities
and needing to connect both the central activity,

00:02:54.860 --> 00:03:01.770
the policy activity, with the activity in
the regions, and I think that has really given

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:06.950
us all a lot more confidence that all of these
priorities are capable of being delivered

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:15.360
and will be delivered successfully.
Clearly, as we go into the next phases – we

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:23.120
have been very much in setup, and it is very
important work on developing strategies – but

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:27.270
it is the implementation that will really
count. The implementation and the financial

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:34.709
implications of some of these priorities are
what is going to exercise us. You will also

00:03:34.709 --> 00:03:40.660
recognise, of course, many cross-interdependencies
between them. I think the ones that we have

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:44.870
always talked about: again, cancer and learning
disabilities have big interdependencies with

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:50.610
information and data and with finance, so
these will all be complexities that we will

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:57.379
be trying to manage as we go through.
Those are the business plan priorities. The

00:03:57.379 --> 00:04:01.550
second part of the report covers the risks.
I will not go into that in more detail; you

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:08.440
have seen the Risk Report before. We continue
to manage and mitigate risks; as we make progress

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:16.370
on some, other risks continue to escalate,
but I think you will probably recognise that

00:04:16.370 --> 00:04:22.590
most of the risks in there are indeed things
that we talk about on a very regular basis,

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:27.720
either around this board table, certainly
at our executive team meetings, so we are

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:32.460
actively trying to manage and mitigate each
of these risks.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:39.510
The third element of the report covers some
aspects – and it is obviously not comprehensive

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:46.600
in any way – of our corporate operations
and processes, and we have tried to pick out

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:54.729
those aspects which are of particular interest
and relevance at the moment; so of course,

00:04:54.729 --> 00:05:04.530
staff turnover, for example, following our
recent change programme, as a number of redundancies

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:12.710
have flowed through the system. Contact centre
progress: I am happy to say that, although

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:20.660
we do have one red rating on the complaints
resolved within 40 days, we are still not

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:26.150
on target for that, but we are improving,
so I just want to reassure you that things

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:31.600
are getting better on that, and we have a
lot more work to do to improve our performance.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:42.759
I will not go into the other detail, but I
am happy to take questions on any of those

00:05:42.759 --> 00:05:47.669
elements.
Just a tiny comment on the contact centre.

00:05:47.669 --> 00:05:55.250
That level of response that quickly after
an IT implementation is really good, so well

00:05:55.250 --> 00:06:00.330
done to your colleagues and everyone.
Thank you.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:07.960
Thank you very much, Karen.
It is overall a really good report; thank

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:13.060
you very much. Just on building the foundations
for improvement in the information revolution,

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:23.900
it would be useful to have just a summary
on the security aspects, the resilience within

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:28.380
the system, in the next report.
Very good, I will do that.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:29.250
Thank you.

